      "title": "Qt: Add filter buttons to QToolBar as QActions",
      "message": "Qt: Add filter buttons to QToolBar as QActions\n\nQToolBar only adds items to the extension menu pop-up used when\nthe width is too small if they are added as QActions and QToolBar\ncreated its own QToolButton for them. If we create our own\nQToolButton and add it as a widget (or use a QWidgetAction), it\ndoes not add them to the extension window.\n\nNote that the default behavior is QToolButton::MenuButtonPopup\nwhich does nothing if the button text is pressed, only if the\nmenu symbol (downwards pointing triangle) is pressed. When we\ncreated our own QToolButton we made pressing the text also\nopen the menu. That seems much harder with the button created\nby the tool bar internally. However, having buttons not appear\nat all is worse.\n\nFix #19887.\n",
      "author_name": "John Thacker",
      "author_email": "johnthacker@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2024-06-18T12:31:45.000-04:00",
